    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "body": "## Bug\n\nAO notifies a worker the first time a tracked PR becomes conflicting, but does not notify it when that conflict is resolved and a later base-branch advance makes the same PR conflicting again.\n\n**Reported from:** AO worker session `agent-orchestrator-149` while handling PR #4165\n**Observed:** 2026-08-26\n**Analyzed against:** `4cbb4b6ce`\n**AO:** locally built `dev`, daemon healthy on port 3001\n**Confidence:** High\n**Priority:** P2 \u2014 missed automation notification; the user can manually steer the worker as a workaround.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Track an open PR owned by a live worker session.\n2. Make the PR conflicting and allow the SCM observer to deliver the merge-conflict nudge.\n3. Rebase the PR so it is clean/mergeable.\n4. Advance the base branch so the same PR becomes conflicting again.\n5. Observe that AO does not deliver a second merge-conflict nudge.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`backend/internal/lifecycle/reactions.go` queues merge-conflict nudges with key `merge-conflict:<pr-url>` and the constant signature `conflicting`. `sendOnce` persists that key/signature in `pr.last_nudge_signature`.\n\nA later non-conflicting observation does not clear or re-arm the merge-conflict dedup entry. When conflict returns, `sendOnce` sees the same key/signature and treats it as already delivered. The persisted state makes the suppression survive daemon restarts.\n\nLive state for PR #4165 confirmed:\n\n- durable mergeability: `conflicting`\n- seen signature: `merge-conflict:https://github.com/Untrivial-ai/agent-orchestrator/pull/4165 = conflicting`\n- attempts: `1`\n\nThis exactly explains why the first conflict notification arrived and the later one did not.\n\n## Fix\n\nRe-arm the merge-conflict reaction after a definitive non-conflicting observation (but not an `unknown` transient): remove/reset that PR-specific seen signature and attempt count, persist the updated reaction payload, and add lifecycle plus observer integration coverage for:\n\n`mergeable -> conflicting (notify) -> mergeable (re-arm) -> conflicting (notify again)`\n\nIdentical consecutive conflicting observations must remain deduplicated, including across daemon restart.",
